    <body>
      <div type="work" n="141">
        <pb n="186"/>
        <head>141 — i — III. — <quote>Because the Lord hath done a wonder</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">On the Holy <persName>Babylas</persName>, Bishop of <placeName>Antioch</placeName> and Martyr, and on the Three Boys Who Were Martyred with Him.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">Let no man be surprised at seeing that <persName>Babylas</persName> the old and advanced in days, a man bowed down from<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> length of time went down boldly to the arena (<foreign xml:lang="grc">στάδιον</foreign>) and to the conflict of martyrdom, and the boys of immature age<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> and their mother<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/>; but let him praise <persName>Christ</persName>, the Word of God, who [after the simi<pb n="187"/>litude of<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> boys shared in blood and flesh<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> and became man without variation, and so far helped and strengthened our feeble race that even persons of tender age receive<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> crowns of victory in the conflict against the devil, who aforetime proudly boasted and said, <quote>I will go up to heaven, and above the stars of heaven will I set the seat of my kingdom; and I will be like unto the Most High</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/>. Let us all therefore in thanksgiving [send up<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> praise to him who by means of his<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a10" target="#n10" n="10"/> Cross dissolved his power; and let us cry to him, <quote>Lord of all, praise to thee!</quote></ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 186, n. 3</orig></choice> Ps. xcviii, 1 LXX.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 186, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>by</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 186, n. 5</orig></choice> Marg. <foreign xml:lang="grc">ἀώρους</foreign>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 186, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>mother of these</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 187, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>similarly to</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 187, n. 2</orig></choice> Heb. ii, 14 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 187, n. 3</orig></choice> Unintelligible corr.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 187, n. 4</orig></choice> Is. xiv, 3-15 <quote>And it shall be..... above the stars of El will I set my seat...... to the Exalted. And hereafter thou shalt go down to <placeName>Sheol</placeName> and to the bottom of the pit</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 187, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>sing a song of</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 187, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>the</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
